 has received less  attention amid a pandemic and a  cratering economy  but 2020s wildfires are say scientists  historic  and there will be more of them in the  future eric sorensen global news  a huge fire has broken out at beirut's  port rattling nerves after last month's  catastrophic blast  the military says it was sparked when  cooking oil caught fire and spread to a  tire warehouse  crews are battling the blaze from the  air and on the ground but there are no  concerns of an explosion  and no injuries have been reported on  august 4 more than 2 700 tons of  ammonium nitrate exploded  killing nearly 200 people and injuring  more than 6 000 others  a widespread cleanup is still underway  in greece help is on the way for  thousands of migrants left without  shelter after a fire destroyed their  camp  today aid was handed out to the many who  have lost everything  about 13 000 people had been living in  squalor at the camp which was meant for  only 3 000 people  greece is sending three ships to the  island to provide shelter for  some as well as emergency tents germany  and france say they'll take in about 400  miners  whose parents aren't with them  the white house in damage control coming  up the damning revelations that  president trump purposely tried to  mislead the american people  about the pandemic  the white house is in damage control  mode tonight over revelations the  president  deliberately misled americans about the  seriousness of kova 19.  donald trump insists he downplayed the  threat to protect the public  but as jackson proskow explains his  actions are just one part of the failure  by the u.s  to effectively fight the pandemic why  did you  lie to the american people and why  should we trust what you have to say  terrible question and the phraseology i  didn't lie  as president donald trump tries to  manage a crisis of his own creation  he's left on the defensive over his  failure to share key information about  the severity of covet 19.  i don't want to jump up and down and  start screaming death  death because that's not what it's about  trump now claims he did the american  people a favor by downplaying the threat  even as he acknowledged to journalist  bob woodward that the virus was far  worse than the flu  this is more deadly this is five per  you know this is five percent versus one  percent and less than one percent  you know so this is deadly stuff if  americans had been told that initially  dr peter hotez believes they would have  taken the pandemic  far more seriously there's a consequence  the american public never  really fully understood or appreciated  the gravity of  the coven 19 epidemic until they started  seeing  family members and friends get sick or  hospitalized  today more than 190 000 americans are  dead  the u.s economy is struggling and  there's still a debate  fueled by trump about preventative  measures like face masks and  restrictions on gatherings  that could save even more lives it had  the effect of turning this into what was  one of the worst  public health disasters in modern  american history  into something even bigger which is a  homeland security threat  the question is whether voters will care  michigan's governor gave a preview of  the argument democrats are likely to  make  they knew they didn't tell us trump  isn't taking the bait insisting he's  better suited than  anyone to lead during this once in a  generation crisis  expert or not we're not doing any more  shutdowns  trump is holding firm even as his  country records more cases and more  deaths  than any other nation on earth jackson  proskow global news  washington still ahead from stylish spy  to queen of thorns the career of the  late diana rigg  the entertainment world is mourning a  legend british actress dame diana rigg  has died by the way are you busy just  now  not today i've just written an article  for the science  weekly but that's finished in the 1960s  she played the elegant secret agent  emma peel on the avengers he loves me  instinctively insurance  intensely rigg then went on to play a  secret agent's wife in the james bond  film  on her majesty's secret service in that  role she was the only bond girl double  07 ever married  in 1994 the queen made her a dame  commander  the equivalent of sir for her service to  the arts  for today's audience she may be better  known as another dame  there are always lessons and failures  yes  you must be very wise by now  brig appeared in 18 episodes of game of  thrones as the scathing matriarch  lady olenna tyrell she stars in a period  drama series slated to come out later  this year  and a thriller set for 2021. her  daughter says she was battling cancer  for the past six months  diana rigg was 82 years old  the music world is mourning the talent  behind this dance favorite  celebration was one of the signature  songs from cool in the gang  ronald bell the singer songwriter and  saxophone player at the heart of this  funky music  has died when belle and his brother  robert cool were growing up in ohio  they couldn't afford drums so they  collected paint cans and taught  themselves percussion by how much paint  was left in each one  his other hit jungle boogie was part of  a musical career that lasted more than  50 years  ronald bell was 68.  up next raptors fans take over jurassic  park and  for good reason  the pandemic has made for a very  different playoff experience this year  all games are happening in the nba  bubble fans are not allowed to attend  but people are still finding ways to  celebrate safely  horns were honking last night at the  drive-in version of the jurassic park  fan zone in toronto you can bet the lot  will be filled again tomorrow night when  the raptors take on the celtics in a  must win  game seven the winner goes on to the  eastern conference final  and that is global national for this  thursday i'm robin gill  tonight your canada is lake cowhich in  bc we would love to see your corner of